[{"slug": "kansas-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights", "title": "Kansas Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: Rules for Selling a Rental", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Kansas Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: Rules for Selling a Rental</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Kansas</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Kansas Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Kansas Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights sale</li><li>Turn the Kansas Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Kansas House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Kansas statutes set the basic rules between landlords and tenants, including deposits, notices and what happens when a rental is sold.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Security deposit limit: one month&#x27;s rent for an unfurnished unit; 1.5 months if furnished; plus up to 1/2 month&#x27;s rent extra if pets are allowed. (K.S.A. 58-2550(a); <a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/058_000_0000_chapter/058_025_0000_article/058_025_0050_section/058_025_0050_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Landlord must return the balance of the deposit within 14 days after determining the amount of deductions, and in no event more than 30 days after termination of tenancy, delivery of possession and tenant demand; wrongfully withheld amounts carry damages of 1.5 times the amount withheld. (K.S.A. 58-2550(b),(c); <a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/058_000_0000_chapter/058_025_0000_article/058_025_0050_section/058_025_0050_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Month-to-month tenancy ends by written notice by either party to terminate on a rent-paying date not less than 30 days after receipt; week-to-week needs 7 days. (K.S.A. 58-2570(a),(b); <a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/058_000_0000_chapter/058_025_0000_article/058_025_0070_section/058_025_0070_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Landlord may enter at reasonable hours after reasonable notice to inspect, repair or show the unit to purchasers; no fixed number of hours stated; entry without consent allowed for extreme hazard. (K.S.A. 58-2557; <a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/058_000_0000_chapter/058_025_0000_article/058_025_0057_section/058_025_0057_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Landlord must comply with building and housing codes affecting health and safety and keep electrical, plumbing, sanitary, heating and air-conditioning appliances supplied by the landlord in good working order; supply running water, reasonable hot water and heat. (K.S.A. 58-2553(a); <a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/058_000_0000_chapter/058_025_0000_article/058_025_0053_section/058_025_0053_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Landlord may not retaliate by raising rent or decreasing services after the tenant complains to a code agency or the landlord, or joins a tenants&#x27; union; tenant has a defense to possession actions. (K.S.A. 58-2572(a),(b); <a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/058_000_0000_chapter/058_025_0000_article/058_025_0072_section/058_025_0072_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Kansas?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Kansas houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/kansas-eviction-notice/'>Kansas Eviction Notice: Types and Days</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/kansas-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Kansas guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-kansas/'>We buy houses in Kansas</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/058_000_0000_chapter/058_025_0000_article/058_025_0050_section/058_025_0050_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>K.S.A. 58-2550(a)</a></li><li><a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/058_000_0000_chapter/058_025_0000_article/058_025_0070_section/058_025_0070_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>K.S.A. 58-2570(a),(b)</a></li><li><a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/058_000_0000_chapter/058_025_0000_article/058_025_0057_section/058_025_0057_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>K.S.A. 58-2557</a></li><li><a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/058_000_0000_chapter/058_025_0000_article/058_025_0053_section/058_025_0053_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>K.S.A. 58-2553(a)</a></li><li><a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/058_000_0000_chapter/058_025_0000_article/058_025_0072_section/058_025_0072_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>K.S.A. 58-2572(a),(b)</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Kansas Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Kansas\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-kansas/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Kansas Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/kansas-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Kansas Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights", "rank_math_description": "Kansas landlord tenant law and tenant rights: deposits, notices, entry and selling a rented house. Official sources only.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "kansas tenant rights"}, {"slug": "kansas-eviction-notice", "title": "Kansas Eviction Notice Rules: Notice Types, Days and Selling the House", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Kansas Eviction Notice Rules: Notice Types, Days and Selling the House</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Kansas</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Kansas Eviction Notice Rules: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Kansas Eviction Notice Rules sale</li><li>Turn the Kansas Eviction Notice Rules offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Kansas House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Kansas law requires a landlord to give a specific written notice before filing an eviction, and the number of days depends on the reason.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Nonpayment: landlord may terminate if tenant fails to pay within three days after written notice (three consecutive 24-hour periods; add 2 days if mailed). (K.S.A. 58-2564(b); <a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/058_000_0000_chapter/058_025_0000_article/058_025_0064_section/058_025_0064_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Lease violation (material noncompliance): written notice that the agreement terminates not less than 30 days after receipt if breach is not remedied in 14 days; repeat breach allows 30-day notice without cure. (K.S.A. 58-2564(a); <a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/058_000_0000_chapter/058_025_0000_article/058_025_0064_section/058_025_0064_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>No-cause end of month-to-month tenancy: written notice, termination on a rent-paying date at least 30 days after receipt. (K.S.A. 58-2570(b); <a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/058_000_0000_chapter/058_025_0000_article/058_025_0070_section/058_025_0070_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Holdover tenant: landlord may bring an action for possession; willful holdover can recover up to 1.5 months&#x27; rent or 1.5 times actual damages. (K.S.A. 58-2570(c); <a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/058_000_0000_chapter/058_025_0000_article/058_025_0070_section/058_025_0070_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Removal is by the person named in the writ of restitution (anyone authorized to serve process), executed within 14 days, reasonable force allowed. (K.S.A. 61-3808; <a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/061_000_0000_chapter/061_038_0000_article/061_038_0008_section/061_038_0008_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Kansas?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Kansas houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/kansas-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>Kansas Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/kansas-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Kansas guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-kansas/'>We buy houses in Kansas</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/058_000_0000_chapter/058_025_0000_article/058_025_0064_section/058_025_0064_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>K.S.A. 58-2564(b)</a></li><li><a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/058_000_0000_chapter/058_025_0000_article/058_025_0070_section/058_025_0070_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>K.S.A. 58-2570(b)</a></li><li><a href='https://www.kslegislature.gov/b2025_26/laws/061_000_0000_chapter/061_038_0000_article/061_038_0008_section/061_038_0008_k/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>K.S.A. 61-3808</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Kansas Eviction Notice Rules, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Kansas\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-kansas/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Kansas Eviction Notice: Types and Days\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/kansas-eviction-notice/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Kansas Eviction Notice: Types and Days", "rank_math_description": "Kansas eviction notice rules: notice types, required days, which court hears the case and selling a rental. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "kansas eviction notice"}]